      CookingSession, CookTimer, SubstitutionEvent, OutcomeFeedback.
    Shape matches spec §4.11, §4.13–§4.15. Step 4 does NOT add VoiceTurn
    (spec §4.12) — that lands in step 6 with the Gemini Live wiring.

    CloudKit compatibility rules applied across all entities (same as step 2):
      * No unique constraints.
      * All attributes optional at the schema level; required-ness enforced
        by Swift repositories + view models.
      * No custom transformers. Collections stored as JSON-encoded Binary
        Data attributes (sourceAssetIds, constraintJSON, pantrySnapshotJSON,
        localNotificationIdsJSON); scalar lists as newline-delimited Strings
        (cautionTags).
      * Nullable Bools (spec §4.14 accepted Bool?) are modeled as a String
        enum with empty-default: "" = undecided, "accepted", "rejected".
        CloudKit-safe pattern per step 2 baseline.
      * Core Data's entity-name "Timer" would collide with Foundation.Timer.
        Using "CookTimer" as the entity name; class name matches. Spec
        §4.13 is the schema reference regardless of Swift class name.
